WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.230
Gastas Ray

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.230
Gastas Ray!

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.260
Is everyone all right?

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.810
Yeah...

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.010
That sure freaked me out, though.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.510
Darling, guys... stay alert!

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.510
Fall back for now!

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:27.370
Mina!

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.810
You fool! Don't just stand there! Run!

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.080
You stupid son!

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.460
Why did you save him?

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.470
You knew it would put you in danger.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.100
Why? There's no reason.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.350
Kiri is my son. That's all.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.600
It's only right to protect your family.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.260
The blood of Chronos purifies Horologues.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.360
Even if you eat me,

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.460
my blood will make sure...

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.930
you go with me!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:06.640
I won't let you lay a finger on 
my darling or my stupid son!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:14.920
Mina!

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.750
Damn it! Is there nothing 
we can do but watch?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.340
What else are we supposed to do, though?

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.860
There's not a single move 
we can make right now!

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.320
<i>The blood of Chronos...</i>

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.380
You stupid son!

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.480
Stupid son, huh?

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:05.030
She tried her hardest to protect 
not only Victor, but me, too.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:07.430
Isn't there...

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.450
Isn't there a way?

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.140
A way to protect Mina

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:13.520
while defeating Aiks?

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.280
<i>Victor's cards... puddles...</i>

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.030
<i>That's it!</i>

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.910
Victor, lend me a hand!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.690
Huh? Huh? What'd you say?

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:33.960
Explain it again!

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.890
I knew you were my son.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.930
In that case, we can protect Mina...
no, your mother...

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.760
and defeat Aiks at the same time.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.130
Two birds with one stone!

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:44.750
Victor!

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.590
I'm sorry.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.520
I don't have many memories of my mother,

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:57.190
so I couldn't understand how you've felt 
since we came to Couljours at all.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.110
A mother is something irreplaceable,

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.550
but all I could think about was my duty.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.920
You're definitely a Virgo. 
Sensitive and prudent.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:16.960
I'm not going to blame you for 
that now, after all this.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.460
I'm your father, aren't I?

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.530
Well, ready to work together 
as father and son?

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.940
Darling?! How...

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.080
You'll know soon.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:38.410
Wait!

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.050
Fools.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.190
Slow Down!

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.450
Why? Why isn't my attack digesting them?

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.200
Just as we figured.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.210
The many puddles of rainwater around here,

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.800
and Victor's dark-backed cards...

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.710
Put one on top of the other,

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.530
and you have an instant mirror!

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.950
It's a simple trick,
but with a massive effect.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.500
Your attack digests 
everything your eyes see.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.720
That should include you,
once you're reflected in a mirror!

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.050
<i>By eating my own time,</i>

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.940
<i>I've reverted to the time 
when I had a human form?</i>

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:23.720
Kiri!

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:24.550
Victor!

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.000
True Rain of a Thousand Camps!

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.410
Ace Spring!

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.090
They did it!

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:38.540
Wh-What the hell is that?!

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.290
Such remarkable power...

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:03.770
I know that it's my main eating 
organ you're all aiming for.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:08.930
If you destroy this, all of your time 
will be returned to you, after all.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.030
However...

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:15.830
Did you really think I would 
keep my most vital eating organ

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.260
in a place where you could easily see it?

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:22.040
You thought it was in my mouth 
all this time, didn't you?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.020
It's truly unfortunate for you,

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:28.280
but I moved it to another 
part of my body long ago.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.050
I'm surprised.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.910
Even in that melodramatic form,

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.010
you'd still use such underhanded methods.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:38.770
Then we only need to crush 
your whole body to bits!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.360
I see.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.820
You still don't get it!

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:45.770
What?!

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.240
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:57.830
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:27.310
Please don't get the wrong idea.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.860
You people interfered in 
my observation of humans,

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.000
and for that, I can't let you live.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.510
You had no chance of winning 
in the first place.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.140
Is everyone alive?!

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.370
Yeah, somehow...

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.690
I'm... fine.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.200
No prob—

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:50.000
<i>It's no use. The rest of them
clearly can't fight anymore.</i>

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.310
<i>Think, Victor! There must 
be a way to beat him!</i>

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.890
<i>At this rate, they'll all...</i>

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.140
<i>die!</i>

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.640
Is human strength just not enough to beat him?

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:05.810
If we had the power to control an 
opponent's body, like Aisrehdar,

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.850
would we have a chance?

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:13.030
<i>Wait. Just maybe...</i>

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.220
What do you think of my idea?

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:33.630
No! It's too dangerous!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.090
Shh. Not so loud.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.600
What—

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.860
What are you thinking?

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.720
If your idea fails, you're dead!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.120
No, even if it works,
you might not come out unscathed!

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.870
But if it does work, we can beat him.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.640
And we might even get back 
the time he stole from me.

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.440
Do you know of another way?

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:56.380
But...

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:01.130
Once a Horologue consumes time, 
it disappears in sixty seconds.

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:04.290
Once that happens,
there's no way to get it back!

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:05.700
Snake told us that!

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.080
Well, then, what about Couljours?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.650
Aiks spit up the time he'd had inside him,

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.950
and Couljours returned to its rightful form.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.210
That got me thinking.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.970
Horologues don't just 
digest the time they eat.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:25.990
They must be able to save it, too.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.230
Don't you think it's worth a try?

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:32.440
No! Absolutely not!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.760
Good grief.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.210
This is the problem with you Virgo prudes.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.970
You would risk your life again
based on a theory,

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:45.170
with no guarantee that it'll work?

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:48.910
Happiness doesn't grow on top of sacrifice.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:53.750
Being family means supporting each other
and overcoming trials together!

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.630
This is what Eve was talking about, Victor.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.790
You think you can do everything on your own,

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:04.370
and you don't even think about the 
feelings of those you leave behind!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.750
This plan depends on how much 
I can trust my friends,

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:20.200
and most of all, how much I can trust you.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:23.520
As your father,

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:26.000
I trust you, my son.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:27.710
So...

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.610
I entrust my life to you.

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:35.840
Take care of it, Kiri.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:40.170
Darling!

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.350
What did you guys talk about?

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.220
What is he...

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:46.200
It's okay. Have faith in him.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:49.090
He will beat Aiks for sure.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.960
You must be getting hungry by now, huh?

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:07.080
What does that mean?

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.680
This whole time, you've just 
been spinning your wheels,

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:13.540
eating houses and earth and things 
that don't fill you up at all, right?

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:14.540
So...

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.090
Have some refreshments, on me!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.380
Eat your fill!

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:21.470
Darling?!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.060
How utterly foolish.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:31.790
However, if you choose death,
I won't stop you!

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:33.350
<i>Got him!</i>

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.630
Darling!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.720
Slow Down!

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.870
Right from the start, the UNIQUE here has been

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:59.330
using immense power to stop my own 
time from flowing out of me!

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.550
What do you think will happen 
if that power is unleashed?

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.300
What?

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:07.140
I'll be able to Slow Down your body itself!

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:10.850
You would sacrifice your own life's time?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.360
<i>It's flowing out faster than I expected!</i>

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:19.570
Darling!

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:20.380
Don't!

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.850
Why are you stopping me?! He's going to die!

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.490
Listen to me, Mina.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:28.670
What?!

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:33.870
If I do this, I can expose the main 
eating organ that Aiks has been hiding.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:37.840
Then you, Mina, and Blaze 
will attack it all at once.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:38.750
No!

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.570
If you're wrong, we won't 
have a second chance!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.260
I can't make that wager!

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.700
You blocked with your right hand, huh?

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:49.930
Habits can't be changed so easily.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:55.180
Aiks is more likely to use his main 
eating organ when in immediate danger.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.450
Hang on!

00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:00.440
Even if it's "more likely,"
that still leaves room for exceptions!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.090
I'm a gambler.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.440
What good am I if I turn down 
a do-or-die game like this?

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.200
For real? That's a damn crazy thing to do.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.830
Now! Mina, Blaze!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.430
Instant Destruction by Fire!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:20.580
Instant Destruction by Fire

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.770
Great Kamaitachi!

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:23.840
Great Kamaitachi

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.270
True Rain of a Thousand Camps!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:27.340
True Rain of a Thousand Camps

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:35.510
Humans...

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:39.390
So this is an emotion other than fear.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.180
How truly wonderful.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.500
We did it!

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.150
Darling?

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.040
Darling, where are you?

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.360
Look there!

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:30.390
Darling!

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:31.240
Victor!

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:34.580
No...

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:42.340
Hey, this ain't good! Where'd he go?!

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:43.960
Did he actually disappear?!

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:45.930
But we defeated Aiks.

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:46.920
Why?

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:49.180
Where's the time he ate?!

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:52.730
Darling...

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.920
No! No! Darling! Come out!

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.540
Darling's time!

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:04.940
No! Don't leave!

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:06.570
Slow Down!

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.570
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:07.790
Slow Down!

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:09.330
Slow Down! Slow Down!

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:11.240
Slow Down!

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:16.750
It's no use. An Oath of Time 
only works on objects.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.330
I know that!

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:22.830
Tell me what else I'm supposed to do, then!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.830
Mina, calm down!

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:28.620
Why?! Why didn't you stop him?!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.340
Why did you let him give 
his life to do this?!

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:34.240
Why?! Why?!

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:42.050
<i>Kiri... Mina... Blaze...</i>

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.030
<i>What happened to me?</i>

00:16:47.010 --> 00:16:48.230
<i>What is this?</i>

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:51.330
<i>Oh... Right.</i>

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:52.970
<i>I'm going to disappear...</i>

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.070
<i>I have to get back, fast!</i>

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:02.430
<i>It's no use! It's too far!</i>

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.030
Give me back my darling!

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:06.560
Give it a rest!

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.350
Don't you think his son is 
hurting more than anyone?!

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:10.840
Don't be ridiculous!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:14.090
How can he be his son?! 
He let my darling die!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:25.090
<i>Oh, dear.</i>

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:28.400
<i>Looks like my gambler's luck just ran out.</i>

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:29.660
<i>Kiri...</i>

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:31.490
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.270
Vic.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.140
<i>Mom...</i>

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.530
To work together with your friends,

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:43.540
to trust them, and to claim victory.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:47.040
You now know what a true victor is.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:47.950
Yeah...

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.510
But this is the first and last time.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:53.050
I'm going to be with you guys now.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.300
You can't.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.300
Victor, you mustn't come here.

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.580
Where you must return to isn't here.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:06.700
It's to your friends... 
no, to your new family.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:11.070
You can hear their voices, can't you?

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:15.800
Victor! Come back!

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.840
Darling!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.820
Victor!

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:20.170
Darling!

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.280
Come back!

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:23.890
Dad!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.290
Dad... What am I supposed to do without you?

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:32.730
All I've done for so long is 
fight to get your memories back.

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:35.800
So what am I supposed to do now?!

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.780
Live, Victor.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:47.280
We'll always be watching over you, Vic.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:56.490
H-Hey...

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.800
Victor?

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.900
I think you mean "Dad," don't you?

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.770
Darling!

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.540
I was so worried!

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.660
I saw you crying, you know.

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:38.280
It was actually cute.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.530
Wh-What are you... saying?

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:45.680
I thought I could finally 
get some good rest,

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:50.110
and then you woke me up screaming,
"Dad! Dad!"

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:53.380
I said... no such thing!

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:55.290
So, uh, what?

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:59.450
Victor slugged Aiks's eating organ, 
then only his clothes were left...

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:01.190
And then... wait...

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:05.580
I was worried about you.

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.080
Victor, the town is already...

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:33.090
<i>That's right... Mom's gift 
to celebrate my adulthood...</i>

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:36.750
<i>I'm 27 years late, but I 
finally got to accept it.</i>

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.400
Couljours?

00:20:56.710 --> 00:21:00.330
I thought that place was 
reduced to ruins years ago.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:04.410
And you just came from there?
You guys have some strange taste.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:12.540
<i>Strange taste, huh? That may be true.</i>

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.650
Hey!

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:15.580
What are you doing?!

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:19.290
<i>Jeez... Those guys just don't understand 
the sentimentality of traveling.</i>

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:21.800
Get over here now!

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:21.800
We're gonna leave you here!

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:22.780
Hurry up!

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:31.550
We made it.

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:35.690
We almost missed boarding 
because of you! You virgin!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.750
Mina.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.460
Kiri's just a child, so there are lots 
of things he doesn't do in time.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:41.280
Like going to the potty.

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:44.630
Don't make it sound like I peed myself!

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:47.130
And he can't even eat 
pasta through his nose.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:48.640
That has nothing to do with it!

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:52.700
What?! He can't even eat 
pasta through his nose?

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:53.750
Pathetic!

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.830
Pasta through your nose? I can 
eat it through my butt—

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:58.330
Shut up, Blaze!

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:20.600
It isn't over yet.

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:21.360
What isn't?

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:23.450
Getting your time back.

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:27.200
Since you still look like that, Aiks...

00:22:27.690 --> 00:22:30.100
...must still be alive somewhere.

00:22:30.100 --> 00:22:32.070
Boy, is he ever stubborn.

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:35.370
Do you regret it?

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:37.620
Missing a chance like that?

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:41.230
There'll always be more chances.

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:44.860
All we need to do is keep 
moving toward the future.

00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:48.730
<i>Time that's passed will never return.</i>

00:22:49.390 --> 00:22:52.950
<i>But, even if everything is lost,</i>

00:22:52.950 --> 00:22:55.130
<i>as long as you have those 
you hold dear to you,</i>

00:22:55.610 --> 00:22:59.400
<i>and your bonds with those 
around you now in your heart,</i>

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:02.320
<i>you can always take off 
toward the future again.</i>

00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:06.660
<i>I can believe that with all my heart now.</i>

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:09.910
So, Kiri...

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:13.340
Eat this pasta through your nose.

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:16.080
What does that have to do with it?

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:18.630
It's long, thin pasta that's 
connected to the future.

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:19.670
Shut up!

00:23:20.050 --> 00:23:23.090
For crying out loud... You never change.

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:24.670
That's the problem with children.

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:27.740
Not changing is much harder 
than changing, you know.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:31.050
Fantasy Future

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:34.260
Fantasy Future

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:34.300
Fantasy Future

00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:34.390
Fantasy Future

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:34.470
Fantasy Future
